{
  "_comment": [
    "Records pyrxd's encoder produced that the REFERENCE TypeScript implementation",
    "accepted, at the commit pinned in hashmark_upstream_pin.json. Do NOT hand-edit,",
    "and do NOT regenerate them from pyrxd alone — regenerating without re-running",
    "the reference decoder turns a cross-implementation result into pyrxd agreeing",
    "with pyrxd, which is the exact failure this repository has shipped before.",
    "",
    "WHAT WAS RUN, 2026-09-18, against cdonnachie/hashmark.rxd @ 866f2b9c (MIT), after",
    "verifying all six pinned file digests matched the clone:",
    "  1. decodeHashMarkScript(script)             accepted every record;",
    "     every field below came back identical.",
    "  2. canonicalAttestationMessage(record)      reproduced canonical_statement",
    "     byte for byte.",
    "  3. verifyAttestation(record, genesis)       recovered the committed signer",
    "     with @noble/curves and returned signer_address below.",
    "  4. encodeHashMarkScript({...})              re-emitted script_hex byte for",
    "     byte from the same fields — HASHMARK_PROTOCOL.md 4.1's requirement that",
    "     two independent encoders produce identical bytes.",
    "127 assertions, 0 failures, plus 5 negative controls his decoder refused.",
    "",
    "The signing keys were throwaway (os.urandom(32)) and were not retained: these",
    "records are byte fixtures, not a wallet. Every record is signed for MAINNET and",
    "none was ever broadcast."
  ],
